  "case_reason": "The counterexample describes an LLM designed to support online inference (matching the subject) that fails to meet specific latency constraints (sub-100ms) under specific conditions (resource-constrained edge hardware during peak traffic). The literal assertion claims the system is designed to support online inference by meeting these latency constraints. The case provides a concrete instance where the design intent exists but the condition (meeting constraints) is not met due to external factors (hardware/resources/traffic). This refutes the absolute claim that the design inherently guarantees meeting the constraints in all deployment scenarios, specifically addressing the 'by meeting' clause as a guaranteed outcome rather than a conditional capability.",
